WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.350
Game of Thrones is one of the bloodiest shows
on television, and it's taken some serious

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:08.970
creative liberties with the source material,
especially since it's now surpassed the timeline

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.840
in George R.R. Martin's books.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.780
With a body count that continues to climb
with every episode, there've been quite a

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.300
few characters to bite the dust on the show,
even if they're still alive and well in Martin's

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.300
world.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.330
Here are some of those dead Game of Thrones
characters you may still read about in The

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.960
Winds of Winter.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.560
Catelyn Stark

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.630
On the show, Catelyn Stark's sad tale ended
when her throat was slit by the Freys at the

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.630
Red Wedding.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.969
In the books, though, she's still kicking
around—although we're not sure you could

00:00:34.969 --> 00:00:36.589
call her "alive."

00:00:36.589 --> 00:00:40.940
Instead of letting Catelyn rest in peace after
she was brutally murdered, George R.R. Martin

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.339
had the Freys throw her body into the Green
Fork of the Trident.

00:00:44.339 --> 00:00:49.409
She drifted downstream until being discovered
by the direwolf Nymeria, who was being unconsciously

00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:50.989
warged into by Arya Stark.

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:55.430
Nymeria pulled Catelyn from the river, and
she was later found by Beric Dondarrion and

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.440
the Brotherhood Without Banners.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.590
After Thoros of Myr refused to revive her
because she was three days dead, Beric gave

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:06.090
Catelyn the kiss of of life himself, bringing
her back at the cost of his own life.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:10.070
Undead Catelyn became Lady Stoneheart, the
new leader of the Brotherhood who set forth

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:15.299
on a bloody campaign of vengeance against
anyone even remotely associated with the Freys,

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:17.000
the Boltons, or the Lannisters.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.119
Although Game of Thrones hasn't been shy about
reviving people from the dead -- even ones

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:24.490
that were already starting to rot like The
Mountain -- Lady Stoneheart has never gotten

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.469
to come out to play and slay on the show.

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:28.580
Ramsay Bolton

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:32.469
Game of Thrones fans may have breathed a sigh
of relief when the "King of Cruel" finally

00:01:32.469 --> 00:01:34.630
bit the dust in Season 6.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:38.929
Ramsay Bolton's death finally gave Sansa Stark
some satisfactory revenge against her tormenter

00:01:38.929 --> 00:01:42.630
and served up some payback for all the times
he'd sicced his dogs on other people.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:47.219
In the books, though, Ramsay is still alive
and wreaking havoc on Westeros right alongside

00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:48.569
his dad Roose.

00:01:48.569 --> 00:01:52.820
Ramsay last appeared in A Dance with Dragons
after wedding Sansa's friend Jeyne Poole—a

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.640
steward's daughter that Littlefinger "trained"
to impersonate Arya.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.310
Several weeks after their nuptials, a still-alive
Mance Rayder disguised himself as a bard named

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:06.049
Rattleshirt to help Theon and Jeyne flee Winterfell
before they ran into Stannis Baratheon's army.

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:10.739
Later, Jon Snow, who didn't know Ramsay's
bride wasn't the real Arya, received a letter

00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:14.230
from Ramsay, demanding the return of his wife
and Reek.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:18.190
Ramsay claimed to have defeated Stannis' army
and slain Stannis himself.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:20.150
Since we know how much Ramsay loves to lie
…

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.909
"I grew up on a salt cliff, my lord.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:25.389
I was only a boy when they took you away."

00:02:25.389 --> 00:02:29.269
… It would be smart to take the Bastard
of Bolton's words with a grain of salt until

00:02:29.269 --> 00:02:31.180
we learn the truth in book six.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.630
Which means we should probably consider Stannis
as still among the books' living for now as

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:36.630
well.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:37.860
Shireen Baratheon

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.880
There's no doubt that Stannis Baratheon is
a cold man in the books and on the show, as

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.830
his thirst for power comes at the expense
of his affection for his wife and daughter.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:49.390
But the show version of Stannis was so much
worse than it had to be.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:54.480
In season five, the red witch Melisandre convinced
Stannis and his wife Selyse to allow her to

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:59.160
sacrifice Shireen to the Lord of Light so
he might bless Stannis' army and lead them

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.280
to victory against the Boltons.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:06.970
Instead, half of Stannis' army deserted him,
Selyse hung herself, and Ramsay Bolton easily

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.459
wiped out the remaining soldiers in battle.

00:03:09.459 --> 00:03:12.650
All while poor Shireen became a pile of dust
on her pyre.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.970
For readers, the sacrifice scene was probably
a shock, since Stannis didn't take Shireen

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:19.239
with him to confront Ramsay in Martin's version.

00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:24.420
In fact, Shireen, Selyse, and Melisandre were
all left behind at Castle Black when his army

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.170
marched with instructions that the Princess
should be left in charge if he fell.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:32.959
As far as we know, Shireen's still kicking
it in her castle, even if her gray scale scars

00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:34.340
frighten the wildlings.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.489
According to the Game of Thrones showrunners,
though, Shireen's fiery death was one of three

00:03:38.489 --> 00:03:42.290
secrets that Martin revealed to them about
the future of his books.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:46.269
So, even if living through Shireen's demise
once was enough, it might happen again on

00:03:46.269 --> 00:03:47.959
paper soon enough.

00:03:47.959 --> 00:03:48.959
Alliser Thorne

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:54.300
At the end of season five, Alliser Thorne
managed to organize a successful mutiny against

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.689
Jon Snow and murdered him to claim the title
of Lord Commander.

00:03:57.689 --> 00:04:02.400
His reign was short, however—after Melisandre
resurrected Jon and the Wildlings captured

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.150
the mutineers, Jon executed them Alliser for
his betrayal.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:10.959
In the books, Alliser still intensely dislikes
Jon …but he's wisely avoided giving Jon

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:12.890
any excuse to execute him.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:16.620
"I never once disobeyed an order.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.890
Loyalty is the foundation upon which the Night's
Watch is built."

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:25.190
In fact, Thorne was still away from the Wall
when the mutineers killed Jon, so he had no

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:26.760
part of their treachery.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.320
If Jon does get resurrected in the books,
then he'll no doubt execute the mutineers—but

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.620
Alliser Thorne won't be on the gallows with
them.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:39.400
"If I had to do it all over, knowing where
I'd end up, I pray I'd make the right choice

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.400
again."

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:41.940
Tommen Baratheon

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:47.000
At the end of Season 6, King Tommen gave new
meaning to the name of his homestead, King's

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.000
Landing.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.610
After his wife Margaery and the entire crowd
at the Sept of Baelor were blown up by his

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:55.670
mother Cersei he lept from his window at the
Red Keep and fell to his death.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:59.700
While there was a tragic end for the young
king on the show, he's still alive and seated

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.700
firmly on the Iron Throne in the books—for
now, at least.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.770
The book version of Tommen is several years
younger than he is on the television series,

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:11.170
and his primary hobbies are signing anything
the small council puts before him and playing

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:12.880
with the kittens Margaery gave him.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:16.950
Speaking of his lady wife, she's also still
alive in the story, and while the two are

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:21.030
married in the books, they most definitely
have not consummated their marriage bed.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:25.280
As of A Dance With Dragons, Tommen's future
rule was looking bright with his uncle Kevan

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:30.430
as Hand and Regent, but Varys nipped that
in the bud when he murdered Kevan and Pycelle

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.220
Considering that the prophecy about Cersei's
children dying in shrouds of gold still looms

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:39.200
large for all the Lannisters, Tommen's death
is probably imminent on paper as well.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.990
Myrcella Baratheon

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:45.430
Unlike most of the Lannisters, Myrcella was
actually a sweet and courteous princess who

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:50.220
was flourishing in Dorne and was quite obviously
in love with Prince Trystane.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:54.610
In Season 6, though, Myrcella became one of
the first victims of Ellaria Sand and her

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:55.610
daughters.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:06:00.320
In her thirst for vengeance over Oberyn Martell's
death, Ellaria gave Myrcella a poisoned kiss

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.900
that later took her life in her uncle-slash-father
Jaime's arms.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:08.040
In the books, however, Myrcella is alive in
Dorne, albeit gravely injured.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:13.000
Cersei sent one of the Kingsguard to bring
her back to King's Landing, but Prince Doran's

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:17.370
daughter Arianne abducted her in an attempt
to have her crowned in opposition of Tommen.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:21.960
In a confrontation with Doran's guardsmen,
one of Arianne's accomplices tried to murder

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:26.830
Myrcella to force a war with the Lannisters,
but instead of killing her, his sword maimed

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.750
her by cutting off her ear and leaving a nasty
scar on her face.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:35.910
As of A Dance with Dragons, Myrcella was traveling
back to King's Landing, accompanied by Nymeria

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:39.160
Sand—who will be taking a seat on the Small
Council.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.530
Rickon Stark

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:44.380
On the show, Rickon Stark joined his oldest
brother Robb in death when he was killed by

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.360
Ramsay Bolton to kick off the Battle of the
Bastards.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:51.890
He'd taken refuge with the Umbers, but that
house betrayed him by pledging fealty, and

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.550
turning him over, to the Boltons.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:54.630
Poor Rickon.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.380
In the books, some of Rickon's story remains
the same.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:01.470
Osha took him and Shaggydog, and they split
from Bran's group in order to keep the Stark

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:02.750
siblings safe.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:06.751
Last we heard of him in A Dance With Dragons,
he'd fled across the Bay of Seals, where Ser

00:07:06.751 --> 00:07:09.950
Davos Seaworth was set to go retrieve him.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:10.950
Hodor

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.620
Hold the door!

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:17.340
Even though Hodor was given a devastating
backstory and final moment in Season 6, the

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.950
gentle giant is still alive and well in the
books.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:24.520
In A Dance With Dragons, Bran, Meera, Jojen,
Hodor and Summer reached the cave of the Three-Eyed

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:25.520
Raven.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:29.590
Although they were attacked by wights just
as they arrived, everyone survived the encounter,

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:32.990
and Bran hasn't encountered the Night King
in any of his green dreams yet.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:37.170
That doesn't mean Hodor will make it through
A Song of Ice and Fire unscathed, though.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:40.660
According to George R.R. Martin, while the
meaning of his name will be the same in the

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.540
books, the way its origin is revealed will
be different.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:47.900
Knowing Martin, that probably means it'll
be just as heartbreaking, though.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.670
Lancel Lannister

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:53.130
Cousin Lancel's future on the show went up
in smoke when he was killed in the season

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:54.430
six finale.

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:58.880
After being dispatched by the High Sparrow
to find Cersei, Lancel spotted one of Qyburn's

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:03.600
child spies and followed him into the labyrinth
of passages below the Sept of Baelor.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.820
There, the child shanked him and left him
to watch as a puddle of wildfire ignited to

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.210
burn him and the whole Sept of Baelor.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:14.540
In the books, Lancel was gravely injured in
the Battle of the Blackwater, leaving him

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.880
a frail and pious man after his recovery.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:21.470
He joined the Faith Militant as a member of
the Warrior's Sons, an order of knights sworn

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:22.550
to serve the High Septon.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:26.610
And when he last appeared in the books, it
was to serve as an escort for Cersei during

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.610
her walk of atonement in A Dance With Dragons.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:32.969
So, whether he'll still be punished by way
of wildfire remains to be seen, which also

00:08:32.969 --> 00:08:38.269
leaves the fates of the High Sparrow, Margaery,
and Ser Loras in question for now as well.

00:08:38.269 --> 00:08:39.620
Walder Frey

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:44.060
While fans of the show had to wait several
years for it, Lord Walder Frey finally got

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:48.160
his comeuppance for the events of the Red
Wedding when he was killed by Arya Stark in

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.759
the season six finale.

00:08:49.759 --> 00:08:54.189
She murdered his sons Lothar and Black Walder
before baking them into a pie and serving

00:08:54.189 --> 00:08:57.579
it to their father while disguised as a serving
wench.

00:08:57.579 --> 00:09:01.620
After she revealed herself and killed him,
Arya took his face and posed as Lord Walder

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:05.899
in order to organize a feast for the remaining
Frey kinsmen—where she murdered them all

00:09:05.899 --> 00:09:07.889
with pitchers of poisoned wine.

00:09:07.889 --> 00:09:11.160
Like the fine vintage that ended the Freys,
the scenes were delicious.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.980
"Winter came for House Frey."

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:18.519
As satisfying as all that was, though, Lord
Walder is still hale and hearty in the books.

00:09:18.519 --> 00:09:23.209
As of A Dance with Dragons, the prickly and
treacherous octogenarian was recently wed

00:09:23.209 --> 00:09:24.920
to another young new wife.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:28.700
Somehow, we have to believe winter is coming
for him in the books, too.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:29.700
Olenna Tyrell

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:35.029
The "Queen of Thorns" Olenna Tyrell received
a relatively gentle death by Game of Thrones

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:39.879
standards in season seven, when she took the
painless poison offered to her by Jaime Lannister

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:41.930
after his army sacked Highgarden.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:46.180
Displaying her trademark sharp tongue, the
Tyrell matriarch opted to take the poison

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:50.560
before revealing to Jaime that she was the
one responsible for the murder of his son,

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.560
Joffrey.

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:52.560
"Tell Cersei.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:55.560
I want her to know it was me."

00:09:55.560 --> 00:10:00.459
Like her onscreen counterpart, the book version
of Olenna has taken leave of King's Landing,

00:10:00.459 --> 00:10:03.450
returning to Highgarden the day after Margaery's
wedding to Tommen.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:07.160
She hasn't been seen in the books since A
Feast for Crows, so it's unknown if Olenna

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:11.430
later returned to the capital after her granddaughter
was arrested by the High Sparrow.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.490
For her sake, we hope not.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:15.310
Benjen Stark

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:19.550
Uncle Benjen didn't have a whole lot to do
on Game of Thrones, despite lasting for seven

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:20.550
seasons.

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:24.110
He was mostly just portrayed as that benevolent
uncle who rode in to rescue his nephews from

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.930
certain doom beyond the wall.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:29.949
And after he was toppled by the Night King's
army in Season 7, he's probably not coming

00:10:29.949 --> 00:10:32.200
back for another rescue mission any time soon.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:36.199
In the books, we never actually got a real
confirmation that Benjen was the mysterious

00:10:36.199 --> 00:10:39.750
undead "Coldhands," but all the clues point
to that being the case.

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:44.060
He popped up to save Sam and Gilly from the
wights as they fled south from Craster's Keep,

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:48.040
and he also killed the Night Watch's mutineers
that attacked Lord Commander Mormont.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:51.939
So, while he still can't get past the Wall
because of magical spells, he's probably still

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:56.400
lurking out there in the woods for the next
time the Three-Eyed Raven needs his help.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:57.400
Littlefinger

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:02.220
In the season seven finale of Game of Thrones,
Littlefinger's scheming finally caught up

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:05.290
to him when Sansa decided she'd had enough
of his meddling.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:09.660
With the help of an info-bomb from Bran and
the slicing skills of Arya, Sansa managed

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:14.649
to catch Littlefinger in his own web of lies
and had him executed for treason and murder.

00:11:14.649 --> 00:11:18.889
In the books, however, Littlefinger is still
trying to pull a fast one on people for personal

00:11:18.889 --> 00:11:20.689
reasons over in the Eyrie.

00:11:20.689 --> 00:11:25.520
Following his murder of Lysa Arryn, Littlefinger's
latest plot is to marry Sansa off with Robin's

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:30.350
cousin so that she can ascend the throne when
Robin eventually succumbs to his chronic illnesses.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:34.600
A sample chapter from The Winds of Winter
indicates that Sansa will have mixed feelings

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:39.439
about this arrangement, simultaneously working
to protect Robin while seducing his cousin.

00:11:39.439 --> 00:11:43.629
And since the woods witch prophesied that
Sansa would slay a savage giant, which sounds

00:11:43.629 --> 00:11:47.120
like the sigil of House Baelish, he might
not make it much longer there either.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:49.860
"Should I send word that I'll be delayed?"

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:50.860
Viserion

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:55.540
One of the most shocking moments of season
seven came when Jon Snow's brigade of zombie-captors

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:59.300
had to be rescued from a sea of White Walkers
by Daenerys and her dragons.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:03.449
In the midst of the rescue, the Night King
took aim at Viserion and managed to slay the

00:12:03.449 --> 00:12:08.079
dragon before resurrecting him as a new undead
mount that he could take through the wall.

00:12:08.079 --> 00:12:11.660
In the books, Viserion and his siblings are
safe—for now.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:15.829
One of the Martells tried to capture one of
the dragons but failed miserably, and when

00:12:15.829 --> 00:12:20.709
we last saw Viserion in A Dance with Dragons,
he was happily roasting and eating the plague-filled

00:12:20.709 --> 00:12:24.130
corpses that the Yunkish army were flinging
into Meereen.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.130
Yum.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.910
The rest of the undead

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:30.470
As if those names weren't enough to prove
the Game of Thrones showrunners have an even

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:34.379
heavier hand than George R.R. Martin, some
of the other characters the author has yet

00:12:34.379 --> 00:12:39.830
to kill off include Barristan Selmy, Doran
Martell, Brynden "the Blackfish" Tully, Randyll

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:46.120
and Dickon Tarly, Lady Walda Bolton, the Sand
Snakes, Thoros of Myr, and Wun Wun, just to

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.120
name a few.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:51.779
In other words, if you thought George R.R.
Martin was savage, he's clearly got nothing

